<?xml version="1.0"?>
<CP_Scriptfile date="Jul 8, 2022">
<CPscript title="The KAT Theorem" level="min" >
<description>The Koebe-Andreev-Thurston Theorem tells us that any triangulation K of the sphere has an associated circle packing P on the Riemann Sphere. In practice, this is found by using maximal packings in the unit disc, as this script illustrates. It is recommended that you run the "MaxPackHyp.xmd" script first.</description>
<text> It is recommended that you run the script "MaxPackHyp.xmd" before this one.

Here we start with a random triangulation of the sphere. </text>
<cmd name="*" mnemonic="*" iconname="dnd_multi.png">act 0;Cleanse;infile_read example.p;Disp -w -f;set_rad .025 a;Map 0 1 </cmd>
<text> A copy of p0 is moved to p1 and the vertex of maximal degree (chosen simply for convenience) is punctured out. As a result, p1 is left with a triangulation of a topological disc. </text>
<cmd iconname="psi.png">copy -p0 1;act 1;puncture M;Disp -w -f -ec5t6 b; </cmd>
<text> You can move the packing around on the sphere with the mouse until you see the hole left by the puncture and the blue boundary component.

The maximal packing for p1 is now computed and displayed in p1; this is hyperbolic. The edges define the punctured triangulation; the vertices neighboring the punctured vertex are the horocycle centers on the unit circles. </text>
<cmd iconname="xeyes.png">act 0;copy -p1 0;max_pack;Disp -w -c -f -ec5t6 b; </cmd>
<text> The packing p1 is copied to p2 and projected stereographically to the sphere. </text>
<cmd iconname="kivio.png">copy -p0 2;act 2;geom_to_s;Disp -w -c -f -ec5t6 b;Map 0 2 </cmd>
<text> Simply adding the southern hemisphere (as a circle on the sphere), tangent to all the horocycles, gives a packing of the original complex K. </text>
<cmd iconname="kuickshow.png">act 1;copy -p2 1;add_ideal;Disp -w -c -cfc195 M -f;Map 1 2 </cmd>
<text> The final step typically involves a normalizing Mobius transformation. Here we apply one which puts the centroid of the circle centers at the origin in 3D. </text>
<cmd iconname="mozilla.png">act 2;copy -p1 2;NSpole;Disp -w -c -cfc195 M -f; </cmd>
  </CPscript>
<CPdata>
